{title: The Dove Did Not Return}
{subtitle: Genesis 6:8–10; 6:13–22; 7:1–24; 8:1–14; 8:20–22; 9:8–17}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×16

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Noah found favor in the eyes of the Lord
[Bb]A righteous man, [C]blameless among the [Dm]crowd
[Bb]He walked with God in the [C]dark and the [Dm]storm
[Bb]Shem and Ham and [C]Japheth by his [Dm]side stood
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Bb]The earth was filled with vi[C]olence and [Dm]sin
[Bb]God said the end of all [C]flesh had come [Dm]in
[Bb]Make yourself an ark [C]of cypress [Dm]wood
[Bb]Coat it with pitch, [C]keep the family [Dm]good
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Two of every living crea[C]ture, [Bb]male and fe[Dm]male
Birds of every [C]kind, kept a[Bb]live and [Dm]stable
