[Bb]The floodgates of [C]heaven opened their [Dm]eyes
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Bb]The waters rose and lift[C]ed the ark [Dm]high
[Bb]Drifting on the surface, [C]under the [Dm]sky
[Bb]Fifteen [C]cubits above the moun[Dm]tains' peak
Only [Bb]Noah was left, [C]for the world to [Dm]seek
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
God remembered [C]Noah and sent a [Dm]wind
The [Bb]waters began to sub[C]side, leaving be[Dm]hind
On the seventeenth [C]day of the seventh [Dm]month
The [Bb]ark came to [C]rest, calm and [Dm]strong
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
He [Bb]opened the window and sent out [C]a ra[Dm]ven
[Bb]Flying back and [C]forth, watching the ha[Dm]ven
